## Why This Is Asked

This question validates real-world multi-inference orchestration, cross-account access patterns, and data governance in a single pipeline. It tests understanding of parallelism, stateful retries, cost optimization, and privacy controls.

## Key Concepts

- Step Functions orchestration with parallel branches for concurrent inference
- SageMaker endpoints for document extraction and risk classification
- S3 for structured output storage with versioning and lifecycle policies
- DynamoDB index design for efficient document lookups
- Cross-account IAM roles using STS AssumeRole with scoped permissions
- KMS encryption for data at rest and in transit
- Retry strategies with exponential backoff and DLQ for failure handling
- Cost considerations including endpoint autoscaling, payload optimization, and lifecycle policies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo state machine outline for Step Functions
{
  "Comment": "High-assurance document ingestion pipeline",
  "StartAt": "TriggerParallelProcessing",
  "States": {
    "TriggerParallelProcessing": {
      "Type": "Parallel",
      "Branches": [
        {
          "StartAt": "InvokeExtractor",
          "States": {
            "InvokeExtractor": {
              "Type": "Task",
              "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
              "Parameters": {
                "FunctionName": "${ExtractorFunctionArn}",
                "Payload": { "s3Key.$": "$.detail.objectKey" }
              },
              "End": true
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "StartAt": "InvokeClassifier",
          "States": {
            "InvokeClassifier": {
              "Type": "Task",
              "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
              "Parameters": {
                "FunctionName": "${ClassifierFunctionArn}",
                "Payload": { "s3Key.$": "$.detail.objectKey" }
              },
              "End": true
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "Next": "PersistOutputs"
    },
    "PersistOutputs": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "${PersistFunctionArn}",
        "Payload": { "input.$": "$" }
      },
      "Next": "UpsertDynamoDB"
    },
    "UpsertDynamoDB": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::dynamodb:putItem",
      "Parameters": {
        "TableName": "${DocumentIndexTable}",
        "Item": {
          "documentId": { "S": "${uuid()}" },
          "s3Key": { "S": "$.s3Key" },
          "extractSummary": { "S": "$.extractor.summary" },
          "riskScore": { "N": "$.classifier.riskScore" },
          "flag": { "S": "$.classifier.flag" },
          "timestamp": { "S": "${aws.currentTimestamp}" }
        }
      },
      "End": true
    }
  }
}
```

## Implementation Considerations

| Component | Approach |
|-----------|----------|
| **Parallelism** | Use Step Functions Parallel state to invoke both endpoints concurrently |
| **Encryption** | KMS CMK with bucket key enabled; TLS 1.2+ in transit |
| **IAM** | Cross-account role with sts:AssumeRole and scoped SageMaker/S3/DynamoDB permissions |
| **Retries** | Exponential backoff (3 attempts) with exponential delay, DLQ for persistent failures |
| **Cost** | SageMaker Serverless for intermittent loads; S3 Intelligent-Tiering; payload compression |
| **Privacy** | Bucket policies blocking public access; CloudTrail logging; data retention lifecycle |
| **Observability** | X-Ray tracing, CloudWatch metrics for latency/error rates, SNS alerts for high-risk documents |

## Why This Is Asked

Tests orchestration, edge cases, and cost/privacy trade-offs for multi-service AWS AI pipelines.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven orchestration (S3 → Step Functions)
- Language detection, sentiment/abuse scoring, translation
- PII redaction and data privacy controls
- Idempotency, retries, and error handling
- Observability (CloudWatch, X-Ray, EventBridge) and cost governance

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Comment": "Chatlog ML pipeline",
  "StartAt": "DetectLanguage",
  "States": {
    "DetectLanguage": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::comprehend:batchDetectDominantLanguage",
      "Parameters": {
        "TextList.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.messages[*].content"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.languageDetection",
      "Next": "SentimentAnalysis"
    },
    "SentimentAnalysis": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::sagemaker:invokeEndpoint",
      "Parameters": {
        "EndpointName": "chatbot-sentiment-abuse-endpoint",
        "Body.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[*]"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.sentimentAbuse",
      "Next": "TranslationCheck"
    },
    "TranslationCheck": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [{
        "Variable": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code",
        "StringEquals": "en",
        "Next": "PIIRedaction"
      }],
      "Default": "Translation"
    },
    "Translation": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::translate:translateText",
      "Parameters": {
        "Text.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[*].Text",
        "SourceLanguageCode.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code",
        "TargetLanguageCode": "en"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.translation",
      "Next": "PIIRedaction"
    },
    "PIIRedaction": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "redact-pii-function",
        "Payload": {
          "text.$": "$.translation.TranslatedText ?? $$.Map.Item.Value.messages[*].content",
          "piiTypes": ["EMAIL", "PHONE", "NAME", "CREDIT_CARD"]
        }
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.redacted",
      "Next": "PersistResults"
    },
    "PersistResults": {
      "Type": "Parallel",
      "Branches": [
        {
          "StartAt": "WriteToDataLake",
          "States": {
            "WriteToDataLake": {
              "Type": "Task",
              "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
              "Parameters": {
                "FunctionName": "write-ndjson-function",
                "Payload": {
                  "conversationId.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.conversationId",
                  "originalContent.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.messages[*].content",
                  "translatedContent.$": "$.translation.TranslatedText",
                  "language.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code",
                  "sentiment.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.sentiment",
                  "abuseFlag.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.abuse_score > 0.7",
                  "redactedContent.$": "$.redacted.Payload.redactedText"
                }
              },
              "End": true
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "StartAt": "UpdateDynamoDB",
          "States": {
            "UpdateDynamoDB": {
              "Type": "Task",
              "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::dynamodb:updateItem",
              "Parameters": {
                "TableName": "chatbot-conversations-index",
                "Key": {
                  "conversationId": {"S.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.conversationId"}
                },
                "UpdateExpression": "SET translatedKey = :tk, language = :lang, sentiment = :sent, abuseFlag = :abuse, lastProcessed = :ts",
                "ExpressionAttributeValues": {
                  ":tk": {"S.$": "$.translation.TranslatedText"},
                  ":lang": {"S.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code"},
                  ":sent": {"S.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.sentiment"},
                  ":abuse": {"BOOL.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.abuse_score > 0.7"},
                  ":ts": {"S.$": "$$.State.EnteredTime"}
                }
              },
              "End": true
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "Next": "Success"
    },
    "Success": {
      "Type": "Succeed"
    }
  }
}
```

